            "heading": "2. How to Use",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>Getting professional DTF transfers is simple:</p><p><strong>Step 1 — Print Your Design</strong><br/>Print your artwork onto the coated side of the DTF film using compatible DTF ink.</p><p><strong>Step 2 — Apply DTF Powder</strong><br/>Apply hot melt adhesive powder evenly while the printed ink is still wet.</p><p><strong>Step 3 — Cure the Transfer</strong><br/>Cure the powder using your DTF curing system according to your equipment and powder specifications.</p><p><strong>Step 4 — Heat Press</strong><br/>Place the finished transfer onto the garment and heat press using the recommended settings for your transfer system.</p><p><strong>Step 5 — Peel & Finish</strong><br/>Peel the film according to the film's recommended peel method. A second press may be used when appropriate for your workflow.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
